;; Bundle B0 Showcase — bounded authority (effect_summary, v0.12.0).
;;
;; `verify --obligation-report` emits a per-function `effect_summary`: a sound
;; may-over-approximation of the coarse capabilities a function may reach through
;; its call graph (object-capability "authority"). Informational, orthogonal to
;; trust — it never enters the verified/asserted lattice (authority ⊥ trust;
;; CHANGELOG v0.12.0 B0 entry, commit b2d9c1a).
;;
;; `log-amount` reaches EXACTLY one capability — `stdout` — and nothing else.
;; Its authority is visible and minimal: a reader can see, without running it,
;; the complete set of effects it can exercise.
;;
;;   llmll verify ./bounded.llmll --obligation-report
;;       ->  effect_summary: log-amount exercises ["stdout"]
;;
;; The twin (unbounded.llmll) is its authority opposite: a delegate hole whose
;; reachable capability set is ⊤ ("unbounded") — the over-approximation cannot
;; bound what an out-of-process agent might do.

(module bounded
  (import wasi.io (capability stdout :deterministic false))

  (def-shell log-amount [amount: int]
    (wasi.io.stdout (int-to-string amount))))
